* text=auto eol=lf

# Agent artifacts are content-addressed: their SHA256 is their identity and is
# recorded in opponents/meta/MANIFEST.csv, reports/ARTIFACT_INVENTORY.md and
# the postmortem METADATA files. Git must never rewrite their bytes, because a
# CRLF checkout changes the digest of every single one of them.
#
# This was a live defect: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, every agent file
# in the working tree was CRLF while every recorded digest described the LF blob,
# so `sha256sum main.py` disagreed with the manifest for the whole project.
opponents/**    -text
champions/**    -text
challengers/**  -text
postmortem_champion_000/** -text
postmortem_champion/**     -text
postmortem_hedge/**        -text
counterfactuals/**         -text
research/public_src/**     -text
data/donor_agents/**       -text

*.parquet binary
*.json    -text
